WEBVTT

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:32.250
Tokimune!

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:08.520
Farewell

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.230
We're finally back.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:24.500
I'm starving.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.450
Yeah, I'm pretty sick of eating rations myself.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.400
Okay, let's get this done.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.150
Is he gonna be okay?

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.360
He hasn't woken up once since then?

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:42.980
Nope.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.220
It's been three days.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:45.970
Isn't that bad?

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:48.730
If only I'd...

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.640
Don't talk like that, Okui-san.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.460
It was his decision.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:54.960
Okay, let's go.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.610
Come on.

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:25.510
You saw this coming.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.650
After he fought that new model,

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:32.520
you knew this would happen if he kept fighting.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.110
Right?

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:36.170
Yeah.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.150
This is why the captain

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:41.820
told him not to pilot Argevollen anymore.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:44.410
But we...

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:49.620
I didn't expect this...

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.940
But you knew something awful would happen, right?

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:54.330
So why...

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.090
I couldn't stop him.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.680
No,

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.540
I decided not to.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:25.630
I'm sorry.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:30.620
You two saved me.

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.310
I'm being selfish.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:34.520
No.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.110
I'm the one who should be sorry.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:52.160
I'll be wearing this outfit when we triumph over Arandas.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:54.350
Make sure it looks good.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.480
Understood.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:01.480
Come in.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:08.740
Oh, this is rare.

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:11.400
How have you been, Lontar?

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.060
It's been a long time,

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:14.660
Brigadier General Zarl.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.460
How do you like this outfit?

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.880
It suits you well.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.430
Doesn't it?

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.380
So, are you as busy as ever?

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.230
Quite.

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:25.310
I see.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.510
Glad to hear it.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:29.500
Arandas' defeat is only a matter of time now.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.310
Work hard.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.400
Of course.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:35.840
Your excellency.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:36.600
Hmm?

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:37.520
Ah...

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:43.530
I'd forgotten just how much Intelligence loves their secrets.

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:45.740
Not as much as you.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.140
Me?

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.030
I have no such secrets.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.830
I'm very public about everything I do.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.760
Then I'll make this quick.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.650
From where did you obtain Sturm Alpha?

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.820
From His Excellency Junios, of course.

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:04.440
That's the official story, yes.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.760
You Intelligence types are such boors.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.820
I'm a busy man.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:12.050
Why are you so obsessed with the enemy's new model?

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.530
If we can get our hands on the new model,

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:19.270
we can learn what kind of technology they have.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.330
Right?

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:23.570
So it was you, then.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.690
What are you talking about?

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.280
The person who tried

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:37.830
to get their hands on Argevollen during the attack on the Great Wall.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:44.880
There it was, just as you'd been told.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:48.760
You must've been delighted to find the new model

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.400
that you'd only heard rumors about.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:54.390
I can just imagine the look on your face.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:58.270
So you tried to obtain it at all costs,

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:00.060
failing again and again.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:02.590
That must've been a lot of effort.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:04.320
And?

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:08.740
You came up with a plan to get a different mech.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.250
You joined forces with Viltriveld.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.800
You offered to have Sturm Alpha fight Argevollen

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.480
in exchange for its data.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:21.500
It was a lot of work to figure this out, but it was worth it.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.830
Your talent is remarkable.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:30.050
I'd expect no less from the man I took under my wing.

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:32.830
So what should I do?

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.510
Or, what is it you want?

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:38.520
Nothing.

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:42.290
Let me tell you something useful.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.120
In war, and in politics,

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:47.510
it's not those from influential families who have the power.

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:49.630
It's those who control the information.

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:50.560
What are y—

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.410
Viltriveld...

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:11.090
That's what I believe.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.720
Brigadier General Zarl!

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:23.840
Our parts still haven't gotten here.

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.270
We can't repair anything like this.

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:31.510
All right! The parts for Arge!

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:32.610
We've been waiting!

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:35.580
Stop your work immediately.

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:41.370
Kybernes Manufacturing is about to begin a large-scale repair.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:44.670
Entry by non-personnel is strictly forbidden.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:49.840
What's with them? What jerks.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.630
No non-personnel?

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.910
We <i>are</i> personnel!

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:57.680
We're the ones fixing it with the few parts we get on the battlefield.

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:02.510
Hey, Jamie?

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:05.280
Your engineers just kicked us out.

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:06.140
Have you heard anything?

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.650
Got it. Take care.

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:13.680
She says she doesn't know anything,

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:16.220
and she has bigger problems right now.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:17.720
Tokimune, huh?

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.550
He's still not awake?

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.910
We gained valuable information from the data

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.890
on the fight between Argevollen and Sturm Alpha.

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:29.000
Have we made up for lost time?

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.310
Yes.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:35.700
We were right to give Fordergrunt Inc. access to the U-Link technology.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.390
There's one thing to report.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.260
What is it?

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:43.980
The cause for the delay in Ingelmia's invasion has been eliminated.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.210
Is that so?

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:46.390
I'm glad to hear it.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.150
So who will take over?

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.960
Of course, we've already got someone selected.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:52.900
All right.

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:56.000
We can finally give the go sign.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:03.790
It's been a long time,

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.270
Lontar.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:12.190
Brigadier General Zarl has passed away.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:14.420
Was there an accident?

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:17.120
Yes. An unfortunate accident.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:22.920
The nation has lost a promising future leader.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:28.100
You don't sound disappointed in the slightest.

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:31.030
You shouldn't be mean to younger people.

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:43.070
We value you all greatly,

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:44.990
as well as the missions you plan.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.840
Intelligence values us?

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:49.620
At what price?

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:55.630
Your homeland isn't the only small nation that's been absorbed by Ingelmia.

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:59.510
Brigadier General Zarl is from an old and prestigious family,

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:02.640
and has many connections both domestic and foreign.

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:06.200
He also grew up with His Excellency Junios,

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.980
and has always acted alongside him.

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:12.650
And now he's suffered from an unfortunate accident.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:16.710
Just after that, Intelligence says they value you.

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:19.050
I don't think you need to worry about the price.

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:23.660
So what am I supposed to offer you?

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:25.220
Nothing.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:28.590
Just do what you have been doing.

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:31.290
No matter who takes over for the brigadier general,

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.670
you'll be appointed front-line commander.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:36.500
What do you want?

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:40.860
Prosperity for Ingelmia and glory for His Excellency Junios, of course.

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.970
Junios comes second, huh?

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:47.290
Watch what you say.

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:49.430
Intelligence reports directly to him.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.440
So does the military.

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:55.490
I kind of like that about you.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.430
We're the ones who did this to him.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:17.420
You understand that, right?

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:20.350
There's still time.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:22.590
We should destroy Argevollen.

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:40.950
Ta-da!

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:46.790
That smells so good.

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:49.030
Go on, eat up.

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:50.790
I sure will!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.000
Is it good?

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.440
Your pancakes are the best in the world!

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:11.690
Sis...

00:13:24.590 --> 00:13:25.450
Tokimune!

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:28.760
Senpai!

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:34.530
G...

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:35.710
Good morning...

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:37.170
This isn't a "good morning"!

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:38.590
That's right, Senpai!

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:42.670
Have you two been watching over me the whole time?

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:44.670
Thanks.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.280
Where are we?

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:49.950
A military hospital in the northwest base.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:51.560
Was it just us who got sent here?

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.230
No, it was the whole unit.

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:54.630
Oh, good.

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:56.390
Everyone's safe, then.

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:59.610
Hello, hello. Excuse me.

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:04.310
Suguro-san!

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:05.620
So, you're awake?

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.930
I've brought a medical team.

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:09.870
We're going to check your vitals.

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:14.750
We'll know quickly if it was NR syndrome or not.

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:18.590
Come in.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:26.880
Private Susumu has regained consciousness.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:27.810
All right.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.780
Shouldn't you go?

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:35.770
What could I do if I did?

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:40.900
You can't even bear to look at her brother's face?

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.480
Ingelmia's attacks are continuing.

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:52.240
We've lost a lot of ground,

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:54.000
and many cities.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:57.550
And we've lost you to a ghost from the past.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.800
Private Tokimune Susumu

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:07.460
is perfectly healthy, both physically and mentally.

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:12.000
If anything, my impression is that he seems to have even more energy than before.

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:13.810
This isn't like you.

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:18.300
You like to beat around the bush.

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:20.380
And now you're talking about your impressions?

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:21.570
It's creepy.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:24.160
I haven't changed a bit.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:28.430
If anything's changed, perhaps it's you?

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:29.160
Me?

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:29.830
Yes.

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:31.150
How?

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:33.350
I mean Lt. Samonji.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:38.650
Wouldn't you normally bring him straight here?

00:15:38.650 --> 00:15:43.090
We're both aware of his importance.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:47.960
But you've left him alone for three days.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.770
That is what's creepy.

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:51.600
Harsh.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.650
When I must be.

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:56.600
It's pretty tough to keep fish.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:16:00.590
You need to control the temperature, the water quality...

00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:03.190
This one's especially challenging.

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:06.300
Feed it too much and it gets huge.

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:11.700
And it leaves leftovers that rot and harm the water quality.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.480
There's a right time to feed a fish.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:15.880
Until then,

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:17.940
you just let it swim.

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:24.240
You aren't looking so good, Marshal.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.580
You must be in bad shape.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:29.220
How so?

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:33.200
I just called you Marshal and you didn't say a word.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.230
You hit the nail on the head.

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:40.610
Viltriveld is pulling the strings behind the scenes.

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:45.440
It's been giving technology to both Ingelmia and Arandas.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:49.990
So their goal from the start was to bring two of the same system together to fight, huh?

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:54.370
And then take data from both sides and use it to develop a new weapon.

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:59.730
Codename: Akatsuki.

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:02.000
Its official name is Perphevollen.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:05.880
The code name for the U-Link system at Kybernes

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:07.760
is "Silver Will."

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:10.080
Silver Will...

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:17.170
Transcription: Jamie Hazaford.

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:17.940
Active!

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.040
I'm counting on you.

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:25.950
Right.

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:30.970
You saw the results of the tests yesterday.

00:17:30.970 --> 00:17:35.190
Tokimune-kun's coma had nothing to do with NR Syndrome.

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:37.900
And we're just doing a startup test today.

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:38.960
Don't worry.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:41.120
It's okay.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:42.250
But...

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:51.120
Look at these linkage depth values.

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:53.390
All he did was get inside and they're so high.

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:56.720
But his vitals are stable.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:59.890
It's truly amazing.

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:02.600
If we can understand this phenomenon,

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:06.350
who knows how many soldiers' lives we could save?

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:13.530
What is this sweet scent?

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:21.800
What happened to Sturm?

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:23.110
It's being repaired.

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:24.790
It was badly damaged.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:26.920
You shouldn't move.

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:27.800
Don't get in my way!

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:31.680
I won't let anybody stop me from piloting Sturm!

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:34.220
I won't let it take me over.

00:18:34.990 --> 00:18:37.060
And that's why I'll keep piloting it.

00:18:37.710 --> 00:18:41.050
I'll take it over first!

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:42.520
Wonderful!

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:45.870
What a talented pilot you are!

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:48.240
I'm sure your sister is happy.

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:52.360
So Argevollen really was based on that mech from seven years ago!

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:54.430
You know?

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:56.870
That will save us time, then.

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:01.080
"Silver Will."

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:03.870
Oh, it's a voice password.

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:04.880
Don't worry about it.

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:08.440
Of course, if you said it, you couldn't access it.

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:09.630
I know that.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:16.140
Your sister was the first test subject for the U-Link system.

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:19.390
"The system went out of control

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:22.280
and it became impossible to shut it down.

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:25.740
The subject desired her own death in order to stop it.

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:27.150
And through her death,

00:19:27.150 --> 00:19:30.400
the first U-Link system successfully shut down."

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:35.910
Does the NR in NR Syndrome stand for Nanjou...

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:37.740
Reika...

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:39.080
That's right.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:42.170
The U-Link system began with your sister,

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:44.500
and was completed with you.

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:47.020
This is a wonderful thing.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:10.370
The NR in NR Syndrome

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:12.440
stands for Nanjou Reika.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.720
Did you know that?

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:18.970
I'd guessed.

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:22.840
What do you think?

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:24.750
About what?

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:28.240
That your sister was killed by the U-Link system.

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:32.170
And that you're now piloting it.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:37.040
I wouldn't say "killed."

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.860
It was an accident, I think.

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:44.300
Sometimes, when I'm in Argevollen,

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:47.530
there's this familiar scent, like my sister is right there with me...

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:50.020
That's how it feels.

00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:58.780
The pancakes my sister made were delicious.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:19.930
The look on your face says "that asshole finally called me."

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:21.550
I was born with this face.

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:23.560
Don't be so cold.

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:26.300
There's something I want to show you.

00:21:41.350 --> 00:21:43.960
I'll get right to the point.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:45.330
Join me.

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:50.720
That's a scary face.

00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:52.590
Well, look at this.

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:13.110
We gaze into each other's eyes, open our hearts.

00:22:13.110 --> 00:22:19.330
A cycle of strength and weakness.

00:22:19.330 --> 00:22:25.960
Your eyes must have adjusted somewhat.

00:22:25.960 --> 00:22:32.630
Verbalize though I may,

00:22:32.630 --> 00:22:40.430
I remember that I can't

00:22:40.430 --> 00:22:47.060
rationalize everything

00:22:47.060 --> 00:22:54.240
The world will change, as long as I remain courageous.

00:22:55.490 --> 00:23:02.250
The telepathy I wouldn't have discovered alone,

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:08.380
leads me ahead, behind your dazzling silouette.

00:23:08.380 --> 00:23:15.760
But even so, I'll keep my unwavering gaze on you;

00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:22.350
It'll reach you someday.
